    "s01": { "translation": "The just shall stand with great steadfastness against those who have afflicted them and taken away their labors. Seeing it, they shall be troubled with a horrible fear, and they shall marvel at the suddenness of the unlooked-for salvation, saying within themselves, doing penance and groaning for distress of spirit: “These are the ones whom we once held in derision and as a byword of reproach. We fools esteemed their life madness, and their end without honor. Behold how they have been counted among the sons of God, and their lot is among the saints.”", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w030"], "reason": "idiom" }] }
